<section id="sec-intro" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>Right Triangle Altitude From Sides Calculator</h2>
  <p>Enter the two legs and the hypotenuse to find the altitude in seconds.</p>
  <p>This calculator finds the altitude of a right triangle: the perpendicular distance from the right-angle vertex to the hypotenuse. Enter the two legs, <span set:html={rich('[[a]]')} /> and <span set:html={rich('[[b]]')} />, and the hypotenuse <span set:html={rich('[[c]]')} />, and it returns <span set:html={rich('[[h]]')} /> using <span set:html={rich('[[h=\\frac{ab}{c}]]')} />. The answer comes out in the same unit as your inputs.</p>
  <p>For example, a triangle with legs of 3 cm and 4 cm and a hypotenuse of 5 cm gives <span set:html={rich('[[h=\\frac{3 \\times 4}{5}=2.4\\text{ cm}]]')} />. Note that 2.4 cm is shorter than either leg, which is always true for the altitude to the hypotenuse.</p>
